   "text": "I read the structure in pieces and joined them into one SMILES, then assigned the stereocentres from the (S) labels in the drawing.\n\n**Fragments**\n- **Acryloyl pyrrolidine:** an N-acryloyl pyrrolidine whose C3 (S) carries a C(=O)N(CH3) group.\n- **Valine unit:** an N-methyl valine with an (S) \u03b1-carbon and an isopropyl side chain, linked by its carbonyl to the NH of the next unit.\n- **Phenylalanine-type unit:** an (S) \u03b1-carbon bearing NH and C(=O). Its CH2 leads to a 3-hydroxy-5-aryl phenyl ring.\n- **Piperazic acid ring:** a six-membered ring with NH and N. Its (S) \u03b1-carbon bears the ester C(=O)O, and the other nitrogen is acylated by the phenylalanine-unit carbonyl.\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, attached to the phenyl ring at C5. C3 carries CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2\u2013O, which closes the macrocycle through the ester. C2 carries the pyridine.\n- **Pyridine:** 2-(methoxymethyl), 6-(dimethylaminomethyl), joined to the indole through its C3.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nFor each stereocentre I worked out the CIP priorities and chose the @/@@ symbol that gives S, matching the labels in the drawing. The four centres are the pyrrolidine C3, the valine \u03b1-carbon, the phenylalanine-type \u03b1-carbon and the piperazic \u03b1-carbon.\n\n**Check**\nI checked ring closures and atom counts by hand against the drawing. I did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: C=CC(=O)N1CC[C@@H](C1)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H]2Cc3cc(O)cc(c3)-c4ccc5c(c4)c(CC(C)(C)COC(=O)[C@@H]6CCCN(N6)C2=O)c(n5CC)-c7ccc(CN(C)C)nc7COC"
